Ms. Watson:

I am breaking my own word 
<https://oprdvolunteerabuse.org/record/oprd/01M30GCBNRZCAEMX90B6T5D710/> 
by writing to you. I told your director I would not write anyone at 
Oregon State Parks except her records officer. I intend to recommit to 
that word, but there is something I must place on the record.

You are responsible for the conditions volunteers serve under.

When a park supervisor and her manager targeted me, there was no one for 
me to turn to. As program manager you should have established routes for 
volunteers to safely report misconduct. You were responsible for my 
safety inside your institution and the record shows you reversed the 
offender. You punished the volunteer.

When you learned I had recorded a meeting 
<https://rswfire.com/signal/01JNK2TKG01JTERAMB7J6AKPK1>, it was your 
responsibility to investigate why. Instead you choose positional 
authority. When I called you directly after that, and held my hand out 
to you anyway, I want it on the record: you told me to put my head down. 
And I did, even though your duty was to stop the ongoing harm.

When the park supervisor sent a man to pressure me while everyone was 
away, it was your responsibility to discover who the man was and hold 
the supervisor accountable for targeting a volunteer. When the park 
manager dismissed me with the flimsiest of excuses, dishonoring a 
veteran, and using a homeless man's journal as the justification, and I 
was at my most vulnerable moment, and I again extended my hand to you, 
it was your job to respond with real care and integrity.

It has been 574 days. Listen to what you did 
<https://rswfire.com/signal/01JQ59R3S0SHQ18E23BC0BM696> with that 
responsibility. It may shock your conscience to hear it after so long. 
You ambushed me. You colonized my interior. You further harmed me after 
the harm I had just endured. You took a man experiencing dismissal and 
forced displacement and violated him further. You severed the life he 
built from scratch with his own two hands. And then you spent a year 
privately editing a Word document, making dozens of revisions over hours 
of writing. I mean this with no disrespect: your document is incoherent 
on its face, but placed next to the record 
<https://oprdvolunteerabuse.org/sunlight/> your own hand damns you.

When your deputy director reached for borrowed power, in an impotent 
attempt to bury your actions, your document traveled with him. To state 
police, who targeted me all over again, for the same thing, stemming 
from the same poisonous tree. One of the detectives wrote 
"unfortunately" he couldn't find anything in the archive. They wanted to 
harm me. And you witnessed their attempt to do so. In silence. And all 
of it stems from your responsibility to me.

You harmed me. You are harming me right now. And because of your 
background, you are the one most capable of seeing the harm. When your 
name is placed in sequence on Key Individuals 
<https://oprdvolunteerabuse.org/key-individuals/>, it is clear you are 
the bridge and the glue between the ugliest acts an institution can 
commit against someone. I redacted your name when I redacted the local 
staff, but it was a mistake. I am choosing to return your name to the 
record. You will stand with those I have classified as dangerous to the 
public.

Earlier this year, I released you from personal liability. That promise 
remains. I will take it to my grave. But I will not protect you at the 
expense of the next volunteer 
<https://oprdvolunteerabuse.org/volunteers/>. Until conditions at Oregon 
State Parks are safe for volunteers, the public must be told why they 
are not, and who holds the responsibility to make them so.

That person is you, Allison Watson.

I do not require a response, but the door is open. I'm not the kind of 
man to shut them.

*Robert Samuel White*
